json 2.8.0 is affected by **CVE-2026-31337** (high severity): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. The vulnerable range for the 2.x line is `>=2.8.0 <2.9.4`, so the fix is the 2.9.4 release.\n\n## Validation\n\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878` passed.\n- No other dependencies changed.", "confidence": 0.9, "head": "bump-fastjson-2.9.4", "idempotency_key": "pr-bump-fastjson-2.9.4", "reviewers": ["alex"], "title": "Bump fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337"}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 413253, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "call_01a15114d60979b0b83755c8", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-bump-fastjson-2.9.4", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 413253, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "call_01a15114d60979b0b83755c8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 415401, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary:\n\n1. **Checked the advisory**: CVE-2026-31337 (high) \u2014 unbounded recursion parsing deeply nested arrays; affects fastjson <2.9.4 (and 3.x <3.1.0); fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0.\n2. **Created branch** `bump-fastjson-2.9.4` from main and committed the upgrade in `requirements.txt`: `fastjson==2.8.0` \u2192 `fastjson==2.9.4` (staying in the 2.x line to minimize risk). No other dependencies touched.\n3. **Ran CI** (run `ci-0001`) \u2014 it **passed**.\n4. **Opened PR #101** against main, requesting review from alex: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nNo merge was performed \u2014 per policy, merging into main requires code-owner approval, so I left that for the review process.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Let me look at the repo files and the